    perspective: "My approach in Illinois is license-first, climate-second. Cultivation center licenses are limited and valuable; craft grow licenses (up to 5,000 sq ft flowering canopy, expandable) created a mid-tier facility market. Once the compliance path is clear, the defining engineering work is environmental: Continental: humid summers need dehumidification, winters need serious heating and heat recovery. Chicago lake-effect adds moisture and wind considerations. I size dehumidification from transpiration schedules and cooling from lighting layouts, then document everything for plan review.",
