    h1: "Cannabis Cultivation Facility Design in Ohio",
    kicker: "Ohio \u00b7 Adult-Use Market",
    intro: "Cannabis facility engineering in Ohio starts with the Ohio Division of Cannabis Control: Ohio voters approved adult-use cannabis (Issue 2) in 2023, with sales beginning August 2024. The Division of Cannabis Control regulates both programs while the legislature reworked the statute (SB 56). A fast-converting market where medical cultivators expanded aggressively for adult-use demand. Ohio's large population and limited initial canopy created strong wholesale pricing for early movers.",
    perspective: "My approach in Ohio is license-first, climate-second. The Division of Cannabis Control issues cultivator licenses in levels by canopy size; medical operators received priority for adult-use conversion. Once the compliance path is clear, the defining engineering work is environmental: Humid continental: hot humid summers, cold winters. Lake Erie adds moisture and snow load considerations in the north. I size dehumidification from transpiration schedules and cooling from lighting layouts, then document everything for plan review.",
